#data
# A plain "data/" (trailing slash) rule prunes the whole directory from
# git's traversal, which means nested "!" negations below can never reach
# inside it -- that's why the chapter PDFs went missing on a fresh clone
# even after adding negation rules the first time. Using "data/*" instead
# ignores data/'s direct children as a wildcard, which negation CAN reach
# into. The NCERT chapter dropdown (get_chapter_list() in
# chatbot_utility.py) reads chapter names directly from these PDFs at
# runtime, so they must ship in the repo. Raw PYQ/model-answer PDFs stay
# ignored -- they're only used by the one-time offline vectorize_book.py
# script, never read at runtime.
data/*
!data/class_12/
data/class_12/*
!data/class_12/biology/
!data/class_12/biology/*.pdf
data_original/

