*.bin
.venv/

vector_db

# chapters_vector_db, pyq_vector_db, and model_answer_vector_db used
# to be ignored here, but that means a fresh `git clone` (e.g. on
# Streamlit Community Cloud) has no NCERT/PYQ content to retrieve at
# all -- the app "runs" but Learn/Practice/Evaluate all come back
# empty. They're small (~36MB total for all three), so committing
# them is simpler and safer than trying to rebuild them at deploy
# time. The lines below undo the *.bin ignore rule above (meant for
# downloaded ML model weight files) specifically for these folders,
# since Chroma's own index files happen to also use a .bin extension.
!chapters_vector_db/**
!pyq_vector_db/**
!model_answer_vector_db/**

# Same trap, third time: the bundled sentence-transformers embedding
# model (see scripts/download_embedding_model.py) is exactly the kind
# of "downloaded ML model weight file" the *.bin rule above is meant
# for -- but this specific copy is intentionally committed so
# get_embeddings() in rag_service.py never needs to reach
# huggingface.co at runtime.
!models/all-MiniLM-L6-v2/**

# Same trap, different file: get_chapter_list() in chatbot_utility.py
# reads chapter names directly off these NCERT source PDFs at runtime,
# so a fresh clone with no chapters here shows "No Biology chapters
# were found." The blanket *.pdf rule above (meant for generated
# reports/scratch PDFs) was catching these too -- this undoes it only
# for the 13 real NCERT chapter PDFs, not the raw PYQ/model-answer
# PDFs elsewhere under data/, which are only needed by the one-time
# offline vectorize_book.py script.
!data/class_12/biology/*.pdf

# Runtime data / backups (not source)
student_progress.db
pyq_questions.json.backup


